Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.39,0:00:09.19,Default,,0,0,0,,Yamou, Yamou, Yamou, Yamou,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.29,0:00:10.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Yimou,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.20,0:00:17.13,Default,,0,0,0,,Yamou!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:03.01,0:01:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,When you two lose this duel,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.39,0:01:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,you and your friends will be sentenced\Nto an eternity in this digital dungeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:09.77,0:01:11.85,Default,,0,0,0,,You're the one who's going down, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.93,0:01:14.15,Default,,0,0,0,,I beat you once and I'll beat you again.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.23,0:01:17.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, but now we're up\Nagainst all five of them.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.27,0:01:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.18,0:01:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not alone in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.67,0:01:21.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Now then.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.09,0:01:25.51,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't believe the big five\Nare all in Tristan's body.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.77,0:01:29.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Those business geeks are sharing\Nme like I'm a corporate condo.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.35,0:01:33.69,Default,,0,0,0,,My first maneuver should\Nseem familiar to you, Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:34.09,0:01:36.39,Default,,0,0,0,,The move's called Clear the Courtroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.87,0:01:40.11,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Judge Man's\NDeckmaster ability. Oh, no.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.45,0:01:41.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Not this move.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.77,0:01:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:42.85,0:01:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,First, I'll give up\N1,000 of my life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:48.59,0:01:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Proceed, Your Honor.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.51,0:01:54.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Prosecute all of their monsters\Nto the full extent of the law.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.97,0:01:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All four of our monsters are gone now.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.01,0:02:02.33,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's not all I've done. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.51,0:02:04.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you forgotten already, Joseph?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.83,0:02:09.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Next, you'll both lose 500 life points\Nfor each monster that I've crushed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.59,0:02:19.61,Default,,0,0,0,,This doesn't make any sense.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.89,0:02:23.60,Default,,0,0,0,,It's a virtual copy of the Duel\NMonsters theme park I designed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:26.31,0:02:29.13,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way Noah could\Nhave known about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.49,0:02:33.55,Default,,0,0,0,,The blueprints for Kaiba\Nland are top secret,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.79,0:02:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,and construction isn't scheduled\Nto begin for another four years!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.83,0:02:39.53,Default,,0,0,0,,But it's all right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:39.89,0:02:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Every detail.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.75,0:02:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,They even included my backstage\Nsecurity system. Checkmate. Checkmate.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.77,0:02:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Access to restricted area granted.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.83,0:02:54.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe I'll get some answers in here.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.51,0:03:02.77,Default,,0,0,0,,If they keep this up, I'll\Nnever get my body back. Don't
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.85,0:03:05.59,Default,,0,0,0,,worry tristan yuki and my\Nbrother are gonna win this
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.67,0:03:08.43,Default,,0,0,0,,now that i've cleared the\Nfield of all of your monsters
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.51,0:03:12.77,Default,,0,0,0,,it's time to work on your\Nlife points i call hysteric
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.85,0:03:17.83,Default,,0,0,0,,angel to the stand and now\Ni think our spectators are
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.91,0:03:22.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Really going to enjoy this next\Nmove, especially that little
Dialogue: 0,0:03:22.87,0:03:28.57,Default,,0,0,0,,monkey boy up there time to\Nput this body to good use
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.65,0:03:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,now hysteric angel attack\Njoseph's life points directly
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.27,0:03:43.93,Default,,0,0,0,,well now i remember why i\Nlove you lawyers so much
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.01,0:03:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,If you love that one, just\Nwait till my next move.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.75,0:03:53.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Angel, use my catapult turtle special\Nability to launch yourself at the defendant,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.35,0:03:54.18,Default,,0,0,0,,Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.26,0:03:55.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Joseph Wheeler.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.67,0:03:59.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey! Are you alright?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.95,0:04:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,That jerk.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.25,0:04:03.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey's life points are almost gone.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.29,0:04:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, get up, man.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.47,0:04:08.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you're alright, Joey?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.85,0:04:10.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been better.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.59,0:04:11.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me, Joseph.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.83,0:04:15.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you beginning to understand my\Ndueling strategy or do you need a hint?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.73,0:04:20.89,Default,,0,0,0,,I plan to destroy the weaker Link\Nfirst, then I'll concentrate on Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:21.31,0:04:23.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Is this the part where\NI'm supposed to be scared?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.63,0:04:27.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're just mad because I wiped the\Ncourtroom floor with you in our last duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.37,0:04:28.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson. Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.61,0:04:29.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't flatter yourself.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.65,0:04:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I place one card face down, and then\NI play the magic card, Altar of Mist.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.75,0:04:38.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh no!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.87,0:04:40.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to that card's effect,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:40.63,0:04:41.67,Default,,0,0,0,,after three turns,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.75,0:04:45.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson will be able to play any\Nritual magic card in his entire deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.73,0:04:50.19,Default,,0,0,0,,That will allow him to automatically summon\Na really powerful monster to the field!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.27,0:04:52.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The prosecution rests. Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.03,0:04:54.43,Default,,0,0,0,,About time. Now!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:55.61,0:04:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright! This'll help.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.35,0:04:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Rocket Warrior!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.13,0:05:04.55,Default,,0,0,0,,This little guy packs\Na pretty strong punch,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.63,0:05:08.47,Default,,0,0,0,,but I'm gonna boost his strength even more\Nwith my Deck Master's special ability.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.55,0:05:09.38,Default,,0,0,0,,After all,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.46,0:05:13.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Flame Swordsman came in really handy\Nlast time I laid a hurtin' on Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.15,0:05:15.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, here comes a move\Nthat you might remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.21,0:05:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Thanks to my swordsman's special ability,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.71,0:05:22.49,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll take a thousand of his attack\Npoints and transfer them to my warrior.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.57,0:05:26.37,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Rocket Warrior,\Nattack his catapult turtle!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.37,0:05:33.61,Default,,0,0,0,,I activate Revenge Sacrifice! No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.39,0:05:39.05,Default,,0,0,0,,This card allows me to sacrifice the\Nmonster you just attacked me with,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.27,0:05:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,so consider your Rocket Warrior dismissed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.91,0:05:45.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And I'll use it to summon a new monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.99,0:05:50.17,Default,,0,0,0,,So please welcome to\Nthe stand, Machine King.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.45,0:05:57.57,Default,,0,0,0,,This mechanical menace\Ngains an additional 100
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.65,0:06:00.47,Default,,0,0,0,,attack points for every\Nmachine monster in play,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.57,0:06:01.57,Default,,0,0,0,,including itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:02.07,0:06:04.13,Default,,0,0,0,,The decision is unanimous.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.35,0:06:06.27,Default,,0,0,0,,You two don't stand a chance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.13,0:06:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, you finish this guy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.73,0:06:13.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll try.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.15,0:06:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.06,0:06:16.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to play Desvoltskov.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.47,0:06:20.81,Default,,0,0,0,,but in order to summon it to the field, I\Nneed to sacrifice another monster first.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.89,0:06:22.60,Default,,0,0,0,,And I have no other monsters.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.69,0:06:23.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Not yet, anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.65,0:06:26.89,Default,,0,0,0,,It's my room, so here goes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.61,0:06:29.20,Default,,0,0,0,,This is just what I needed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.45,0:06:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the Rock Spirit monster card.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.51,0:06:32.97,Default,,0,0,0,,But in order to use it,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.13,0:06:37.01,Default,,0,0,0,,I first have to take a monster out of my\Ngraveyard and remove it from the gate.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.09,0:06:39.95,Default,,0,0,0,,I was forced to send Buster\NBlader to the graveyard before.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.03,0:06:42.21,Default,,0,0,0,,so I guess I'll take him out of play.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.55,0:06:43.38,Default,,0,0,0,,First,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.47,0:06:48.73,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll remove my Buster Blader from the\Ngame in order to summon the Rock Spirit.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.21,0:06:51.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But I'm afraid that's not all, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.05,0:06:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll sacrifice my spirit to\Nsummon this Despolt Scout.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.01,0:07:03.84,Default,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.01,0:07:05.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Is he serious?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.37,0:07:09.81,Default,,0,0,0,,And now I'll place a card\Nface down and end my turn.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.67,0:07:11.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.58,0:07:12.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Johnson's on to Yugi's trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.07,0:07:14.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That move was too obvious.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.27,0:07:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,It'll never work.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:21.27,0:07:23.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you think Joey's\Nacting kind of weird?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.93,0:07:26.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I think maybe a bumblebee\Nflew down his pants?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.01,0:07:29.66,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he's trying to warn\NYugi about something.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.67,0:07:33.01,Default,,0,0,0,,See, Yugi played a weaker monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:33.17,0:07:36.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Then he put a card face down,\Nwhich is a really predictable move.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.97,0:07:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,He wants Johnson to attack him. Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:41.03,0:07:43.47,Default,,0,0,0,,That doesn't sound like\Nsomething Yugi would do.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.55,0:07:44.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.63,0:07:48.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Out of the way, Johnson.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.37,0:07:50.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time for a real\Nduelist to take charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.73,0:07:52.45,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm still on this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.65,0:07:55.41,Default,,0,0,0,,So back up, Nesbitt. Quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.75,0:07:59.51,Default,,0,0,0,,It's about time that I stepped\Nin to rewire this duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.11,0:08:01.75,Default,,0,0,0,,I am Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.91,0:08:07.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Now meet my Deckmaster, the unstoppable\Nandroid robotic knight. It's him!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.81,0:08:10.77,Default,,0,0,0,,He's the one who did\Nthis to Tristan. Woo-hoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.39,0:08:12.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare to lose.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.43,0:08:14.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That fool, Yugi,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.81,0:08:18.83,Default,,0,0,0,,has played a monster weaker than my\NMachine King and a face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.91,0:08:22.07,Default,,0,0,0,,It appears he has constructed\Nquite an amateur trap,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.33,0:08:24.79,Default,,0,0,0,,and I think he knows I'm onto him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.03,0:08:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You look a bit nervous.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.13,0:08:30.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Nesbit knows his plan.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:31.03,0:08:34.77,Default,,0,0,0,,Yugi may as well be wearing a sign\Nthat says, I set a trap, so attack me!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.85,0:08:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,First thing I'll do is rid the\Nfield of your face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.53,0:08:40.97,Default,,0,0,0,,So sorry, but take this.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.27,0:08:42.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Heavy Storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:42.45,0:08:46.01,Default,,0,0,0,,It destroys all your magic\Nand trap cards on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.41,0:08:53.89,Default,,0,0,0,,Mirror Force was your face-down card.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.51,0:08:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:55.75,0:09:00.65,Default,,0,0,0,,My plan was to reflect the attack of\NMachine King right back at you, Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.99,0:09:02.27,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on, Yugi.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.39,0:09:04.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the oldest trick in the duel book.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.85,0:09:07.65,Default,,0,0,0,,It was worth a try. Worth a try?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.43,0:09:13.81,Default,,0,0,0,,There's too much at stake here to try a\Nlame move like that, Nuke. All right, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.13,0:09:15.72,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time to dismantle you.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.03,0:09:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Go, Machine King.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:17.61,0:09:18.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.37,0:09:21.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't do it, Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.79,0:09:23.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Disassemble his Desvoltscow.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.45,0:09:27.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you. What?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.25,0:09:31.93,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like you fell for my\Nreal trap, Nesbitt. What trap?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.15,0:09:34.67,Default,,0,0,0,,You have no more trap cards left in play.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.01,0:09:41.69,Default,,0,0,0,,You're obviously unaware of Des Voltscalf's\Nspecial ability, so allow me to explain.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.33,0:09:44.49,Default,,0,0,0,,When you played your magic card,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:44.69,0:09:48.55,Default,,0,0,0,,you increased my monster's\Nattack strength by 200 points,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.83,0:09:51.33,Default,,0,0,0,,giving it a total of 2400!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.91,0:09:55.45,Default,,0,0,0,,And now, Des Voltscalf, attack! He's back!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.31,0:10:03.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Lucky break, kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.99,0:10:06.91,Default,,0,0,0,,And my monster has one more effect.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.17,0:10:11.85,Default,,0,0,0,,When it destroys your monster,\Nyou lose 500 life points, Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.31,0:10:13.85,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not impressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.21,0:10:16.05,Default,,0,0,0,,500 points is nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.35,0:10:20.31,Default,,0,0,0,,I still have plenty of\Nlife points left. You fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.95,0:10:25.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Think, don't you realize what\Nhe just forced you to do? What?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.01,0:10:27.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, I get it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:27.93,0:10:28.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Get what, Duke?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.39,0:10:33.99,Default,,0,0,0,,See, Yugi just tricked Nesbitt into\Nattacking him instead of attacking Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.33,0:10:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You mean because Joey is\Ndown to 300 life points?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.21,0:10:41.53,Default,,0,0,0,,So Joey would have lost\Nthe duel. That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.79,0:10:44.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Without any monsters on\Nthe field to protect him,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.29,0:10:46.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey would have been\Ncrushed by Machine King.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.11,0:10:50.07,Default,,0,0,0,,So that's why Yugi set\Nsuch an obvious trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.31,0:10:53.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Nesbitt was sidetracked,\Nso he forgot Joey.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.11,0:10:55.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice one, Yuge!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.53,0:10:56.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Way to protect Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:57.85,0:10:59.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Your acting was key.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.31,0:11:00.75,Default,,0,0,0,,That made it convincing.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:01.29,0:11:02.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh? Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.51,0:11:03.81,Default,,0,0,0,,So Joey knew!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.07,0:11:05.21,Default,,0,0,0,,He was playing along!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.29,0:11:06.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I'm impressed.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.63,0:11:08.11,Default,,0,0,0,,He managed to fool me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.39,0:11:09.49,Default,,0,0,0,,Good acting, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.43,0:11:13.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Way to fake him out, Joey!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.03,0:11:17.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh, yeah, that was no sweat\Nat all for me, Serenity.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.57,0:11:22.75,Default,,0,0,0,,that was close if it weren't\Nfor yugi i'd be a goner
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.83,0:11:28.03,Default,,0,0,0,,for sure that won't work again\Nit certainly won't because
Dialogue: 0,0:11:28.11,0:11:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,i'm about to step in and\Ntake charge of this body once
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.13,0:11:34.93,Default,,0,0,0,,i eliminate mr wheeler\Ncrushing yugi will be simple
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.27,0:11:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,all right you corporate\Ncreepazoid you're out
Dialogue: 0,0:11:40.37,0:11:42.65,Default,,0,0,0,,of luck pal because\Nother than that walking
Dialogue: 0,0:11:42.73,0:11:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,junkyard you call a deck\Nmaster it looks to me
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.03,0:11:47.68,Default,,0,0,0,,like you're out of\Nmonsters leaving your life
Dialogue: 0,0:11:47.85,0:11:50.69,Default,,0,0,0,,points wide open! Here goes! Ah, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.09,0:11:52.99,Default,,0,0,0,,Panther Warrior, baby! Wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.23,0:11:57.41,Default,,0,0,0,,He can't attack unless I sacrifice\Nanother monster first, and I'm fresh out!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.49,0:11:59.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe dueling every member of the Big Five
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.81,0:12:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,at the same time wasn't such a great idea,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.49,0:12:04.08,Default,,0,0,0,,because if we lose, they'll
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.23,0:12:06.35,Default,,0,0,0,,get all our bodies!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.65,0:12:09.65,Default,,0,0,0,,I summon Panther Warrior in defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.73,0:12:13.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not gonna let these business\Nbuttheads get to my life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:13.67,0:12:16.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll wrap things up by\Nplacing this little number face
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.83,0:12:22.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Down it's all you. You right and\NI know what I need to do. I'm
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.91,0:12:27.73,Default,,0,0,0,,sorry tristan but i must attack\Ndirectly do what you gotta
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.81,0:12:34.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Do Yugi, just don't mess up the hair,\Nit's gonna be fine. Now, Despotska,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.33,0:12:36.17,Default,,0,0,0,,attack his lifepoints directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.21,0:12:46.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I'll summon Big Shield\NGardner in defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.01,0:12:49.35,Default,,0,0,0,,That's all for now, Nesbitt.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.65,0:12:52.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm not Nesbitt anymore, you fool!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.23,0:13:00.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like Noah didn't have enough\Nimagination to fill this place with anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.61,0:13:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, it's another one of that\Ntwerp's virtual doorways.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.89,0:13:11.41,Default,,0,0,0,,If I had to guess, I'd say it\Nleads to more images from my past.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.19,0:13:14.11,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.29,0:13:15.94,Default,,0,0,0,,A cheap old movie projector?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.19,0:13:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Get with the times, Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.13,0:13:26.23,Default,,0,0,0,,I bet you can't catch me, Dad.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.21,0:13:28.17,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Noah.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.59,0:13:30.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Nice outfit, dork.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.41,0:13:35.97,Default,,0,0,0,,How sad. That little twerp is still\Ntrying to convince me that he's Gozaburo.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.05,0:13:41.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Kaiba's son. I'm afraid it'll take more\Nthan a few fake home movies to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:42.57,0:13:43.61,Default,,0,0,0,,What's this?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.31,0:13:45.87,Default,,0,0,0,,How can this have happened?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.95,0:13:51.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't worry. Noah can still be\Nsaved. I'll find a way. But how?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.33,0:13:55.37,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing I can't do. What\Nis all this supposed to mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.61,0:13:58.08,Default,,0,0,0,,That Noah was in some sort of an accident?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.47,0:14:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,It's time you learned the truth, Seto.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.67,0:14:03.73,Default,,0,0,0,,If these images are real,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.93,0:14:06.37,Default,,0,0,0,,then that would mean that\Nsomething devastating happened
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.45,0:14:09.79,Default,,0,0,0,,to Noah right before Gozaburo\Nadopted me and Mokuba.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:10.45,0:14:15.23,Default,,0,0,0,,But why would Noah want me to know all\Nof this information about his past?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.59,0:14:18.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Unless someone else is behind all this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.65,0:14:24.31,Default,,0,0,0,,Alright, say goodbye to\NNesbit and his pathetic robot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.39,0:14:29.07,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm Lector, and I'll be controlling\Nthis body for the remainder of the duel.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.27,0:14:30.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.21,0:14:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Less talking, more dueling.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.75,0:14:34.11,Default,,0,0,0,,Fine. I'll draw. Not quite.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.37,0:14:36.91,Default,,0,0,0,,You triggered my trap. Sorry, Lector.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.41,0:14:38.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Me drop off.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.61,0:14:41.79,Default,,0,0,0,,My card sends the card you\Njust drew to the graveyard.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.21,0:14:43.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Guess again.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.43,0:14:45.47,Default,,0,0,0,,No way!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.89,0:14:47.95,Default,,0,0,0,,What gives?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.23,0:14:49.93,Default,,0,0,0,,How'd you destroy my trap card?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.01,0:14:51.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha ha ha ha ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.71,0:14:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Haven't you noticed the monster\NI've chosen to be my deck master?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.89,0:14:56.81,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Jinzo!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.99,0:14:59.39,Default,,0,0,0,,My trap cards are useless! That's right!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.53,0:15:02.24,Default,,0,0,0,,He'll automatically\Ndestroy every one of them!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.53,0:15:03.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Huh!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.44,0:15:08.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I play the magic card, Pot of Green,\Nallowing me to draw two more cards!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.45,0:15:12.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Excellent!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:12.93,0:15:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.84,0:15:17.30,Default,,0,0,0,,You just played a magic card which\Ntriggers my Vault Scout special ability!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.39,0:15:20.27,Default,,0,0,0,,so it gains 200 attack points.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.65,0:15:22.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.33,0:15:28.01,Default,,0,0,0,,He won't be around for much longer\Nanyway, for I summon my Fairy Lily.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.57,0:15:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,Ha!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.85,0:15:34.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks like she's only got\N400 attack points, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.49,0:15:36.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Looks can be deceiving, Joy.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.59,0:15:40.39,Default,,0,0,0,,I give up 2,000 life points\Nto increase her power.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.37,0:15:43.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Lily, destroy his Desvolt scout.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.29,0:15:53.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That maneuver cost you more\Nlife points than it cost me.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.21,0:16:00.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Not exactly, because I'm about to restore\Nmine with my Sevix Blessing Magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.43,0:16:03.33,Default,,0,0,0,,What's the deal with that card?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.57,0:16:08.99,Default,,0,0,0,,It increases Lecter's life points by the\Nsame number of life points I just lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.83,0:16:10.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Exactly!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:10.93,0:16:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And if my math is correct, that\Ngives me 1,000 more life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.97,0:16:18.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And finally, I'll place\None card face down.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.91,0:16:24.15,Default,,0,0,0,,Soon we'll claim four more of your bodies,\Nleaving your minds trapped here. You!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.41,0:16:26.41,Default,,0,0,0,,We gotta do something and fast!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.45,0:16:30.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Get ready, boys.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.61,0:16:33.23,Default,,0,0,0,,To give up your bodies, there it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.49,0:16:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I've just activated Gravity Bind,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.85,0:16:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,which stops all monsters with\Nfour more stars from attacking.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.33,0:16:42.05,Default,,0,0,0,,That includes everything\Nexcept my fairy lily.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.29,0:16:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,That's a trap!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:43.41,0:16:47.43,Default,,0,0,0,,And your Jinzo's supposed to\Ndestroy all trap cards on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.55,0:16:50.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That's usually true, but\Nsince Jinzo's my deckmaster,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.05,0:16:54.27,Default,,0,0,0,,he only destroys my\Nopponent's traps. Aw, yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.47,0:16:56.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, awesome.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.03,0:17:00.95,Default,,0,0,0,,This body-snatching bozo's about\Nto get a taste of his own medicine,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.03,0:17:02.73,Default,,0,0,0,,because I got a Jinzo, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.07,0:17:06.63,Default,,0,0,0,,I sacrificed Panther Warrior\Nso I can summon this.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.87,0:17:08.23,Default,,0,0,0,,My own Jinzo.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.53,0:17:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Your Jinzo may not cooperate,\Nbut mine definitely will.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.59,0:17:18.73,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, Jinzo, destroy his trap.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.39,0:17:27.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Aw, yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.30,0:17:29.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Celebrating so soon? Yeah, why?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.61,0:17:31.53,Default,,0,0,0,,You may have destroyed my trap card,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.61,0:17:35.25,Default,,0,0,0,,but my fairy lily is still the\Nstrongest monster on the field, Mr.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.33,0:17:40.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Wheeler! Once I power her up again, she'll\Nwipe out your Jinzo and your life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.87,0:17:41.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Eh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.78,0:17:43.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Joey, Lecter is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.59,0:17:46.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Her special ability allows\Nhim to raise her attack
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.11,0:17:48.69,Default,,0,0,0,,points higher than any\Nother monster on the field.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.77,0:17:49.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.87,0:17:53.91,Default,,0,0,0,,But then again, attack points\Naren't everything, are they, Joey?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.49,0:17:55.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait a sec.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.71,0:17:57.39,Default,,0,0,0,,Yuki's trying to tell me something.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.47,0:18:00.57,Default,,0,0,0,,There is a way to crush this guy's\Nmonster before it crushes me.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.65,0:18:03.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Even though Lecter can raise\Nhis fairy's attack points,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.27,0:18:06.37,Default,,0,0,0,,her defense points stay pretty low.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.39,0:18:09.55,Default,,0,0,0,,I play Flock Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.01,0:18:13.78,Default,,0,0,0,,This magic card switches your\Nfairy from attack to defense mode!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.47,0:18:15.81,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.41,0:18:17.91,Default,,0,0,0,,I just did!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.37,0:18:23.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Jinzo, do us all a favor and send his\Nlittle monster back to Fairyland, will ya?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.57,0:18:25.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Cyber Energy Shock Attack!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.55,0:18:31.01,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, that's all for me, Lecter.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.61,0:18:33.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, back to you, Yook.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.45,0:18:34.57,Default,,0,0,0,,Pound this poser.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.27,0:18:36.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.18,0:18:37.61,Default,,0,0,0,,Time to take you down.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.35,0:18:42.61,Default,,0,0,0,,And I have just the card\Nto do it in my head.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:43.73,0:18:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Come forth, Dark Magician Girl!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.55,0:18:49.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Your light points are wide open!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.31,0:18:52.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Dark Magician Girl, attack him directly!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.97,0:19:01.47,Default,,0,0,0,,He just lost 2,000 life points.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.43,0:19:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,It's your move.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.87,0:19:13.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The time has arrived, my young friends,\Nto reap the benefits of my magic card.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:13.81,0:19:14.73,Default,,0,0,0,,Say what, man?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.61,0:19:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, he's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.03,0:19:19.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been three turns since\Nhe played Altar of Mist.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:19.87,0:19:22.81,Default,,0,0,0,,Now he can summon almost\Nany monster he wants.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.01,0:19:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,You are correct.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.95,0:19:30.99,Default,,0,0,0,,What's so funny, Lecter?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.97,0:19:35.89,Default,,0,0,0,,That's getting real annoying.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.21,0:19:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,If you were me, you'd laugh, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.65,0:19:45.79,Default,,0,0,0,,For in my hands, I hold the Big\NFive's most powerful creature.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.31,0:19:48.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Say goodbye to your bodies.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.11,0:20:02.03,Default,,0,0,0,,You're mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.77,0:20:07.35,Default,,0,0,0,,You're mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.23,0:20:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
